## 4. Derived ONNX determination

An ONNX file exported locally from one exact cleared checkpoint is a modified
or derivative form covered by the same Apache-2.0 grant. It is redistributable
only when the release record binds:

- the exact source model ID, commit, tree, checkpoint size and SHA-256 above;
- the exact exporter source/toolchain and command;
- a reproducible output byte count and SHA-256;
- the complete Apache-2.0 text with SHA-256
  `cfc7749b96f63bd31c3c42b5c471bf756814053e847c10f3eb003417bc523d30`;
- a prominent statement that the checkpoint was converted to ONNX; and
- every upstream copyright, attribution or NOTICE item actually present at the
  selected source revision.

Neither inspected model tree contains a `NOTICE` file, so there is no upstream
NOTICE file to reproduce at these revisions. That is not permission to omit the
Apache-2.0 licence text or the modification notice.

The ready-made `csukuangfj/speaker-embedding-models` ONNX files are **not**
cleared by this determination. Their repository still has no licence or
provenance binding from its ONNX bytes to these exact source checkpoint bytes.
They remain `FAIL-CLOSED-UNKNOWN`; local conversion is the only cleared route
unless that mirror obtains its own grant and exact provenance.

## 5. Boundaries and residual risks

### 5.1 No wildcard clearance

Only these two checkpoint digests are determined. The following remain outside
the result:

- every other `iic/speech_campplus_*` model, including 3D-Speaker-trained,
  CN-Celeb, bilingual-advanced, diarization-bundle and language-identification
  repositories;
- every `iic/speech_eres2net*` checkpoint;
- all downstream ONNX mirrors; and
- any future revision or changed checkpoint digest under either model ID.

The broad row in `0.2.1-S0-LICENCE-F104-ASR.md:66,432-452` must not be used as
selection authority. Its exact English and Chinese CAM++ subcases are replaced
by this document; its ERes2Net and wildcard portions remain admission-only and
unknown for selection.

### 5.2 Training data is provenance, not a second grant

The English card says the checkpoint was trained on VoxCeleb2; the Chinese card
says approximately 200,000 Chinese speakers. The primary model-repository grant
is the operative permission over the checkpoint. It does not prove every
training-data chain-of-title fact, transfer rights in the training recordings,
or permission to redistribute the three bundled example recordings.

F104 already excludes the example audio, and this result does not change that.
Only the checkpoint is cleared. If release policy later requires a complete
training-data rights chain rather than an affirmative checkpoint grant from the
publisher, both rows must be reopened.

### 5.3 Biometric/privacy obligations are separate

Apache-2.0 imposes no use restriction, including no restriction on diarization,
speaker verification or voice cloning. That licence result does not waive
privacy, biometric-data, consent, recording, impersonation or jurisdictional
law. F104's explicit-session, local-processing and no-retention controls remain
mandatory product policy rather than licence conditions.

## 6. Selection gate

The English checkpoint may enter P2 comparison under the following exact
conditions:

1. P2 uses ModelScope checkpoint
   `5b1a88b6f8d85826fabef804779c3372b42f3af21457fa48bd5c097c0686b2de`,
   not a mirror or a moving ref.
2. The self-exported ONNX file is reproducible and bound back to that source
   checkpoint and the pinned 3D-Speaker exporter source.
3. F100/F104 package metadata records `Apache-2.0`, `redistributable: true`,
   `use_restricted: false`, and `cloning_permitted: true`, with the qualification
   that the field is a licence determination rather than a technical feature.
4. The complete Apache-2.0 text and conversion notice are present offline before
   the install decision and in any redistributed artifact bundle.
5. No ModelScope example recording and no unlicensed ONNX mirror enters the
   product, test corpus or release artifact.

Failure of any condition fails closed. This document clears licence eligibility;
it does not select CAM++, approve a supported profile, move a consumer pin, or
claim P2 measurement success.

